      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T03:20:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, in the NPCX Port80 module/driver, we get the Port80 code byte-by-byte (via DP80BUF register) even when AP sends it with 4-byte. In patchset 1 of CL:2847668, I just sent what is read from DP80BUF directly to common Port80 layer.\nHowever, per comments, it lost the readability and endianness. So I combined 4 1-byte into a 4-byte code and sent it to the common Port80 (parchset 4).\nWhat do you think if we go back to use patchset 1 of CL:2847668? With it, we don\u0027t need to change the common layer and should be no inconsistent issue.\n(Though, it lose the readability and endianness.)",
      "parentUuid": "217a68ec_b0ea03bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "14dd51f4fcfeb1bbbdbf0dd9f9365c4072db44ef",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
